# AGENTS.md — `metadata/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies. Placement comes from the root
[`README.md`](../README.md) contract.

## Additional constraints

- Schemas may be changed with corresponding tests and migrations. Factual rows
  may be transcribed only from user-supplied or authoritative records; never
  infer sample identities, conditions, files, dates, or execution facts.
- `runs.csv` is append-only. Do not edit, reorder, deduplicate, or repair it by
  hand. Invoke the registration command only after explicit user approval.
- `provenance/<execution_id>.json` is immutable after registration. Never replace
  it or accept the same execution ID with different content.
- A failed or ambiguous registration must fail loudly. It must never leave a
  ledger row without its archive or alter an existing record. An archive-only
  state can remain after a ledger-write failure; verify it and retry the same
  registration so the idempotent tool completes it. Do not delete or improvise
  a partial repair.
- Do not move sample manifests into `lab/` or `data/`. Bench narrative belongs in
  the configured bench record; validated machine mappings belong here.

You may validate schemas/manifests and inspect current or archived provenance
without approval. Validation does not authorize changing a factual record.
